      "content": "While some tenderness and low-grade fever are normal during the first week after gallbladder surgery, worsening pain and new pressure when pressing on your abdomen are concerning signs that could indicate a complication like an infection or leak. Given your symptoms of escalating pain combined with a fever, you should contact your surgeon's office immediately to report these changes. It is best to avoid assuming this is normal healing and seek professional medical advice before the end of today to ensure your safety.",
